B4NxbTmGcV_289J6lORA28-NcomZWAhPs3yBxwIfLKaLjv44v5CJlfqSxmq0gTe9US8SUMo=.eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoib3BlbmFpL2dwdC01LjYtbHVuYS0yMDI2MDcwOXxvcGVuYWkifQ\",\"format\":\"openai-responses-v1\",\"id\":\"rs_0a4ea1244d39f651016af0dec093fc87d1859c3d10da594c9c\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_hGnDmIyOQAEiRqq5N3ZMqar9","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":".ki-base/decisions/0002-render-protocol.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_t5RKVle4ZZjlcy0w62MywBrz","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":"KI_rich_markdown.md","section":"Panel","max_chars":12000}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_pSi8q9NAGnw7hl7qFxFvVQWR","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":"KI_rich_align.md","section":"Measurement","max_chars":12000}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_xSGGTrtCljgowWCtAuMSwSYX","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","arguments":{"rel_path":".ki-base/decisions/0003-style-composition-and-ansi.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":3,"output":173,"cacheRead":5033,"cacheWrite":1502,"reasoning":11,"totalTokens":6711,"cost":{"input":6.000000000000001e-7,"output":0.00020759999999999998,"cacheRead":0.00010066,"cacheWrite":0.0003755,"total":0.00068436,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794170559638,"responseId":"gen-1794170559-RhW96aqlIyjACwrOKnhr","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":2405,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_hGnDmIyOQAEiRqq5N3ZMqar9","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nRich supports arbitrary nested UI components (such as Panels inside Tables inside Trees). If custom components were allowed to mutate shared rendering options or directly manipulate the `Console` buffer, rendering would become non-deterministic, thread-unsafe, and incompatible with real-time displays like `Live` and `Progress`.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Mandatory Console Protocol:**  \n   All visual components must implement the public generator protocol:\n   ```python\n   def __rich_console__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> \"RenderResult\":\n       ...\n       yield Segment(...)\n   ```\n   A component may optionally implement `__rich_measure__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> Measurement` for dynamic sizing.\n\n2. **Strict Component Isolation Invariants:**\n   - **No Buffer Access:** Components must NEVER access or write to `console._buffer` or `console.file` directly. All output must be returned via `yield` as an iterable of `Segment` or renderable objects.\n   - **Options Immutability:** The passed `options: ConsoleOptions` instance is strictly read-only. Components must never mutate its fields. To adjust constraints for child components, use `options.update(...)` which returns a fresh copy.\n   - **Stateless Yielding:** Generators must be re-entrant and idempotent so that multiple render passes (e.g. measuring then rendering) produce identical results without side effects.\n\n3. **Internal Spacing Convention for Inline Badges:**\n   - In accordance with repository design conventions, inline badge components must enclose their inner text with exactly one space of padding inside the boundary caps: `\"( \"` + content + `\" )\"` for pill badges, and `\"[\" + \" \"` + content + `\" ]\"` for square badges.\n   - Example: `Badge(\"DEPLOYED\", pill=True, icon=\"★\")` must yield segments rendering as `\"( ★ DEPLOYED )\"`. Square badges render as `\"[ SYSTEM ALERT ]\"`. Measurement must include the 4 cells occupied by borders and inner spaces.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Components can be composed arbitrarily without side effects.\n- Direct console buffer writes or mutating shared options is treated as an architectural violation and rejected in code review.\n- Ensures seamless integration with `Live` displays and virtual screen buffers.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":42,"timestamp":1794170562119},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_t5RKVle4ZZjlcy0w62MywBrz","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# KI: Rich Core (Markdown, Markup, Panels & Prompts)\n\n## Overview\nProvides markdown document parsing, console markup parsing (`[bold red]...[/]`), framed panel containers (`Panel`), recursive object pretty-printing (`Pretty`), user interactive prompts (`Prompt`), and the Rich Console Protocol definitions.\n\n## Entry Points & Public API\n- `Markdown`: Renderable converting CommonMark Markdown specifications into stylized terminal blocks.\n- `Panel`: Framed container with border styles, title, and subtitle around any renderable.\n- `Pretty`: Recursive data structure pretty-printer handling cyclic references and custom indentation.\n- `Prompt` / `Confirm`: Interactive CLI input prompts with validation, default values, and type coercion.\n- `escape`: Utility escaping square bracket markup tags in arbitrary text.\n\n## Key Components\n| Class / Function | File | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Markdown` | `rich/markdown.py` | AST walker converting markdown elements (headings, code blocks, lists, blockquotes) into renderables |\n| `render` / `escape` | `rich/markup.py` | Parser converting `[tag]text[/tag]` markup strings into styled `Text` spans |\n| `Panel` | `rich/panel.py` | Boxed border container enclosing renderables with titles and alignment |\n| `Pretty` | `rich/pretty.py` | Data structure formatter handling dicts, dataclasses, pydantic models, and recursion |\n| `Prompt` / `Confirm` | `rich/prompt.py` | Interactive console prompt asking questions and verifying user answers |\n| `Measurement` | `rich/measure.py` | Minimum and maximum width calculation protocol (`__rich_measure__`) |\n| `Padding` | `rich/padding.py` | Surrounds a renderable with top, right, bottom, and left whitespace margins |\n| `is_renderable` | `rich/protocol.py` | Introspection helper checking if an object implements Rich protocols |\n\n## Testing & Verification\n- Test commands: `pytest tests/test_markdown.py tests/test_markup.py tests/test_panel.py tests/test_pretty.py tests/test_prompt.py`\n- Test files: `tests/test_markdown.py`, `tests/test_markup.py`, `tests/test_panel.py`, `tests/test_pretty.py`, `tests/test_prompt.py`\n\n## Non-obvious Details\n- **The Rich Console Protocol**: An object is renderable if it defines `__rich__() -> Renderable` or generator `__rich_console__(console, options) -> Iterable[RenderResult]`.\n- **Measurement negotiation**: Containers query children using `Measurement.get(console, options, renderable)` before layout allocation to determine optimal width.\n- **Markup tag stack**: `markup.py` maintains an internal tag stack. Self-closing tags or single closing slashes (`[/]`) pop the most recent active style off the stack.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n- **Unclosed markup tags**: Forgetting to close tags like `[bold]` can lead to unexpected syntax errors (`MarkupError`) if strict parsing is enabled.\n- **Prompt stdin EOF**: Calling `Prompt.ask()` in non-interactive CI environments without mocked stdin results in an unhandled `EOFError`.\n\n\n## Related KIs\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/align.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/box.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/cells.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/console.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_align.md]] (via `rich/containers.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/errors.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/highlighter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_default.md]] (via `rich/jupyter.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/__init__.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/_emoji_replace.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/color_triplet.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_emoji.md]] (via `rich/emoji.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_live.md]] (via `rich/_loop.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_pick.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/_stack.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_null.md]] (via `rich/abc.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/repr.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/rule.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/segment.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_region.md]] (via `rich/style.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/syntax.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/table.py`)\n- [[KI_rich_syntax.md]] (via `rich/text.py`)\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":50,"timestamp":1794170562123},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_pSi8q9NAGnw7hl7qFxFvVQWR","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Section 'Measurement' not found in 'KI_rich_align.md'."}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":70,"timestamp":1794170562133},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_xSGGTrtCljgowWCtAuMSwSYX","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nStyling in terminals requires combining foreground colors, background colors, links, and various text attributes (bold, italic, underline, reverse, etc.). Rich needs an immutable, high-performance styling algebra that supports cascading inheritance, markup parsing, and export to both ANSI terminals and web formats (HTML/SVG).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Immutable Style Class:**  \n   The `Style` object is immutable and hashable with internal caching:\n   - Attributes (bold, underline, double_underline, italic, blink, etc.) use tri-state values (`True`, `False`, `None` where `None` indicates inherit/unset).\n2. **Style Composition Algebra (`+` operator):**  \n   Style addition (`style1 + style2`) cascades attributes from left to right:\n   - Attributes defined in `style2` override attributes in `style1` if set (`is not None`).\n   - Unset attributes (`None`) in `style2` inherit values from `style1`.\n3. **ANSI Sequence Mapping & Exporters:**  \n   Every new style modifier must maintain synchronization across:\n   - Terminal ANSI code generator: open code (e.g. `\\x1b[4:2m` or `\\x1b[21m`) and reset/close code.\n   - Default style definitions (`rich/default_styles.py`).\n   - Markup parser (`rich/markup.py`) to recognize `[modifier]...[/]`.\n   - Exporters (`rich/terminal_theme.py`, `rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots.\n- Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution across nested tags.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"isError":false,"durationMs":63,"timestamp":1794170562142}]}
