ization phase seems crucial.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.summary\",\"summary\":\"**Examining import issues**\\n\\nI'm trying to figure out why there are failures in the tests possibly linked to changes in the environment, especially with pygments. I wonder if changing the import order or adding Text at the top level has affected pygments and syntax coloring. It seems that importing Text early might introduce side effects. I need to be careful to avoid importing Text at the module load level, as it could cause cycles and unexpected behavior. Lazy imports might be a better approach.**Investigating import effects**\\n\\nI'm trying to understand how avoiding the Text import during package initialization might help tests pass more consistently, even though there are current issues with Pygments. I suspect that importing from `rich.text` could be triggering `rich.syntax`, but it isn’t clear how that affects syntax. There seem to be differences in test cards related to the current Pygments theme. It’s possible that earlier tests expected the behavior of Pygments 2.19, but normally, tests pass. Importing Text in the initialization phase seems crucial.\",\"format\":\"openai-responses-v1\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"gAAAAABq8N8VvT9KbyleXRw4svfw2GKy21FX1bZv3YcUR40z_9LnB_fVuy97zGZTb8EwlKvWSEQO2YvxTofAaBs2U220loJqR50rXPDQB4kCLNqMmmJSIsLRnd52mlqrEqzBzLfh7bBmPRzKAKUXzx1opi1S4KXJmMEIrmG8PoQmLmZMiFbdfLzSLcrROadqo2CVmQN9T-XQHEFRC0XFmiouIW_b3ET04ZHCVp-ooxDyWmSrPu8QKvXN-ElSn55ipL69V3VFch2QxeCnUnl8GSGJcdCA24aJO33w96I9MjTaHnV3nty5va1a-ZQ6o5t8zjLpOMtoeEG9W-j_EHiXG2Bmnc76uuUUgfMSKfXqlFV-JYng3iC0OtjylhEHbVJn5G1lUW34Dtoz_Aoyh7bLk4PKXwIzadjLGculC8O_hRzMYs3umnrZ9tZnfxXKUs80aCtGnayBsbjTze9Szd-tlc_-ikAuD5fKRUtUAeLvTqEPRM2C-fgaEtFEgTE-J9mmdM1Vb0LyymMSphxYoIr1rD1gU1OvHjL53vreKXzFzkF7CJpieJYh_lz-jPpYkbL021S-oD3IbgJVmPBKECesCVqDAHUv-e302lXqH-2gxoYQIvnj4KXwIrYp8Pis5nelTqMvAYBlqS50FgN7AljqN0OJ9m489MqfJbdhcHrXbtKvOtr-82JtCQc7qbZ5ED4ixAjkWxxX70JS9B66g09sVN